oints toward the GOP. No general-election polls, expert ratings, or market prices are available for this race yet, so the state's partisan lean anchors expectations. The Republican ticket starts with a clear but not overwhelming edge in a contest with no incumbent president on the ballot.\n\nCoverage through 2026 points to genuine Democratic momentum: midterm and special-election results were described as trouble for Florida Republicans, and analysts flag the state as a 2028 proving ground. Still, the same coverage stresses how difficult reversing the state's MAGA-era shift has been, and Republican primary polling featuring Rubio, Vance, and DeSantis says little about the general election. The expected margin sits in the mid-single digits for Republicans, with wide uncertainty until real polling arrives.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2832, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.3401, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.352, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.3574, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.3329, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.3466, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.3674, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.3674, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.3461, "margin": -4.0}]}